                <pb facs="1118" n="982" sameAs="frus:frus1888p1/pg982"/>

                <head>No. 686.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Thompson to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Port au Prince Hayti</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-11-26"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 26,
                        1888</date>.<lb/>(Received December 10.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 235.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    No. 132 of the 15th instant, and to inform you that your telegram of the 10th
                    instant was transmitted to me by our consml at Kingston, Jamaica, and received
                    by me this morning. Your instructions therein contained had, in principle, been
                    faithfully carried out.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John E. W.
                    Thompson.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
